Dicastery Institutions and resources Administrative Section Cancelleria Via Municipio 13 6850 Mendrisio 058 688 31 10 stationary@mendrisio.ch Res. mun. 5773 of 15.09.2026 18 September 2026 Competition for the recruitment of a Installer or a 100% electric installer, at an indefinite time, at the Municipal Company (AIMsio) of the City of Drinking Conditions

Tasks:

The owner of the function, included in the Drinking Water Section of AIM, AP Plant and Quality Office, will have the following main tasks:

• to collaborate in the phase of study, realization and commissioning of new plants

aqueducts;

• co-ordinate the ordinary maintenance of the plants and the

aqueduct infrastructure in accordance with the provisions of self-control provided for by Swiss food legislation;

• operate as a reference person for fault management, maintenance

ordinary and improvement interventions regarding telemanagement and electrical installations;

• keep the documentation inherent to the plants per day;

• provide availability to participate in the regular picket service.

In addition:

• may be or be given other work assignments compatible with its function

and its skills;

• can be called or called to service at irregular times, even out of time

and on public holidays according to the needs of service. City of Mendrisio Competition

Requirements:

• Federal Certificate of Capacity (AFC) as Electrical Installer;

• experience in aqueducts can be preferential title;

• good knowledge of MS Windows operating system and its MS Office tools;

• good relational, organizational, communication and analytical skills;

• license to conduct category B;

• Swiss citizenship or home in Switzerland.

Preferential securities may be set up:

• availability to obtain the diploma of Fontaniere/a AFP;

• knowledge of a second national language (German or French).

Gross annual wage (including threeteenth monthly and salary scale updated at 01.01.2026):

- Classes (4)* 5 - 7 ROD (Operation/or Artisan Function);

- Minimum: CHF 62’022.-- yearly; (*CHF 58’371.-- yearly)

- Maximum: CHF 85’327.-- annual;

- In addition to the salary is paid, to the entitled, the allowance for children according to

LAFam.

* In case of intake of employees with little experience or for which it is reasonably

necessary to foresee a period of introduction, the City Hall can establish a lower initial salary of a class than the minimum entry class. Within the framework of the above-mentioned possibilities of pay, the City Hall can recognize the activity carried out previously, if conformed to this Chapter, assigning one or more year of service pursuant to art. 29 cpv. 2 ROD.

Working week:

40 hours

Degree of employment:

100%

Start of activities:

As soon as possible.

Deadline for competition:

Applications must be submitted via the application form by Friday 9 October 2026 at 23:59, accompanied by the following documents:

- letter of presentation;

- curriculum vitae with photos;

- copies of study and work certificates;

- self-certification of good conduct and any executive procedures;

- health questionnaire.

Applications submitted in another form will not be considered. City of Mendrisio Competition This notice of competition and its application form are also available on the https://www.mendrisio.ch/concourses. The Human Resources Section remains at the courteous disposal (tel. +41 58 688 33 10) of those who do not have a device (PC, tablet, smartphone, scanner, etc.) to provide them with the necessary tools to send their application through the prescribed application form. In addition to the documents to be attached to the application, at a later time may be required to present the extract of the court for private individuals and the extract of the execution register (validity 6 months). The City Hall reserves the right to change the tasks at any time, in relation to any changes in the regulations and regulations in force. It is the faculty of the City Hall to proceed with a pre-selection of candidates and candidates for the call to hearings. The City Hall reserves the right not to proceed with recruitment, in the absence of candidates or candidates eligible for the function. Legal remedies Against the notice of competition shall be the right to appeal to the Lodging Council of State within 30 days of the date of publication. Detailed information can be obtained from the Directorate AIM, Via Municipio 13, Mendrisio, tel. 058 688 38 00. The Town Hall

